179
00:36:30,911 --> 00:36:31,391
Okay.

180
00:36:31,692 --> 00:36:40,331
And then you have another interpreter that belongs to the programming language.

181
00:36:40,731 --> 00:36:44,911
The interpreter takes the compiled code as an input.

182
00:36:45,612 --> 00:36:45,951
Okay.

183
00:36:45,951 --> 00:36:54,411
And then it transforms that compiled code into an executable code that can run on the CPU.

184
00:36:54,867 --> 00:37:03,087
Okay, so which means that in any interpreted language, so we have an intermediary file, which is a compiled file.

185
00:37:03,087 --> 00:37:08,708
In Java, this intermediary file ends with dot class.

186
00:37:09,448 --> 00:37:09,587
Okay.

187
00:37:10,132 --> 00:37:15,091
So the source code that we are going to write ends with .java.

188
00:37:15,632 --> 00:37:26,152
And then you use the compiler of the programming language and turns this file .java into another file, another intermediary file called .class.

189
00:37:26,963 --> 00:37:27,443
Okay.

190
00:37:27,923 --> 00:37:30,344
And then you use an interpreter.

191
00:37:30,523 --> 00:37:33,724
Again, that belongs to the same language, Java programming language.

192
00:37:33,864 --> 00:37:45,604
The interpreter takes this intermediary file, this dot class file, and it converts into a format, okay, which can be run on the CPU.

193
00:37:46,900 --> 00:37:55,699
And for Java programming language, the compiler is javac.exe. As you see, it's an executable file.

194
00:37:57,119 --> 00:38:04,159
And for interpreter, it is javac.exe. And this is the interpreter.

195
00:38:05,100 --> 00:38:09,180
And so the Java calls this interpreter as Java Virtual Machine.

196
00:38:09,180 --> 00:38:09,940
